@startuml money-distribution-flow
!define STRIPE_COLOR #FFE082
!define BACKEND_COLOR #E1F5FF
!define BANK_COLOR #C8E6C9

' Destination charges + manual capture.
' We DO NOT call stripe.payouts.create — Stripe runs payouts to the
' connected account automatically on its T+7 (TH) schedule.

participant Buyer    as "Buyer (iOS)"
participant Backend  as "Backend"
participant Stripe   as "Stripe\n(platform + connected acct)"
participant Webhook  as "Webhook handler"
participant DB       as "Postgres"
participant Bank     as "Seller's Thai bank"

== Phase A: funds authorized, listing PAID, awaiting pickup ==

note over Stripe
  After webhook flow in diagram 02:
   Payment.status = REQUIRES_CAPTURE
   Listing.status = PAID
   Funds: authorized on buyer's card,
          NOT yet moved.
end note

== Phase B: buyer confirms receipt at pickup ==

Buyer -> Backend: POST /listings/:id/confirm-receipt
activate Backend
Backend -> DB: SELECT listing FOR UPDATE\nassert status in {WAITING_FOR_PICKUP, SENT}\nload Payment by currentPaymentIntentId
Backend -> Stripe: paymentIntents.capture(\n  paymentIntentId,\n  { amount_to_capture: amountSatang }\n)
activate Stripe
Stripe -> Stripe: Move funds:\n  - amountSatang charged to buyer\n  - platformFee  → platform balance\n  - sellerNet    → connected-acct balance\n  (one atomic destination-charge capture)
Stripe --> Backend: PaymentIntent { status: succeeded }
deactivate Stripe
Backend -> DB: Payment.status = SUCCEEDED\n              capturedAt = now()\n              Listing.status = RECEIVED
DB --> Backend: ok
Backend --> Buyer: 200 OK
deactivate Backend

== Phase C: Stripe confirms via webhooks ==

Stripe -> Webhook: payment_intent.succeeded
activate Webhook
Webhook -> Webhook: verify sig + dedupe (StripeWebhookEvent)
Webhook -> DB: ensure Payment.status = SUCCEEDED\n              ensure Listing.status in {RECEIVED, RATED}
deactivate Webhook

Stripe -> Webhook: charge.succeeded
Webhook -> DB: Payment.stripeChargeId = charge.id

Stripe -> Webhook: application_fee.created
Webhook -> DB: Payment.stripeApplicationFeeId

Stripe -> Webhook: transfer.created
Webhook -> DB: Payment.stripeTransferId\n              SellerProfile.totalEarnedSatang += sellerNet

== Phase D: payout to seller's bank (handled by Stripe) ==

note over Stripe
  Stripe automatically rolls up the
  connected account's balance and
  initiates a payout on the account's
  schedule (Thailand default: T+7 business days, THB).
  We do NOT call payouts.create.
end note

Stripe -> Bank: ACH/PromptPay payout in THB
activate Bank
Bank --> Stripe: settled
deactivate Bank

Stripe -> Webhook: payout.paid (Connect event,\n  stripeAccount = seller's acct)
activate Webhook
Webhook -> DB: SellerProfile.totalPaidOutSatang += payout.amount\n              (optional) push notification "เงินเข้าบัญชีแล้ว"
deactivate Webhook

== Live balance (UI) ==

note over Backend
  Seller wallet screen calls:
    GET /sellers/me/balance
      → stripe.balance.retrieve({ stripeAccount })
    GET /sellers/me/payouts
      → stripe.payouts.list({ stripeAccount })
  No local pending/available columns.
end note

@enduml
